INSERT INTO blog_post_translations
  (post_id, locale, slug, title, excerpt, body_html, seo_title, seo_description)
VALUES (
  :post_id, 'en', $x$how-to-buy-ps-store-games-from-uzbekistan$x$,
  $x$How to buy PS Store games from Uzbekistan$x$,
  $x$Which country to pick for your PSN account, why it cannot be changed, which PS Store card fits and how to redeem it on PS5 and on the web.$x$,
$x$<p>To buy games in PS Store from Uzbekistan, you need a PSN account of a specific country and a PS Store gift card of that same country. The card tops up the account wallet, and the wallet pays for games and PS Plus.</p>
<h2>Key takeaways</h2>
<ul>
<li>You choose your PSN account country once, at sign-up. It cannot be changed later.</li>
<li>A PS Store card works only on an account of the same country. A Turkish card is for a Turkish account, a US card for a US account.</li>
<li>Wallet funds are held in the account country's currency and do not move to another region.</li>
<li>Need another country's store? Players create a second account and switch users on the PS5.</li>
<li>YuPay has PSN cards for 43 countries on one page. Pay in soʻm with Click, Payme or Uzum: the total in soʻm is shown before payment, and that is exactly what is charged.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Which country to pick for your account</h2>
<p>Players in Uzbekistan usually use an account of another country: Turkey, the UAE, the USA, Poland and others.</p>
<p>The country decides three things:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>currency and prices</strong> — the Turkish store prices in lira, the US store in dollars;</li>
<li><strong>catalogue and language</strong> — the game list and localisation differ by region;</li>
<li><strong>which cards work</strong> — only cards of that same country.</li>
</ul>
<p>The Turkish PS Store is popular for its prices. But Sony has raised them several times: PS Plus alone went up 55 % in 2025. Compare the price of the game you want across regions yourself, before you sign up, not after.</p>
<p>If you already have an account with purchases and trophies, staying on it is usually simpler. You can see its country in the account settings on the console or on the PlayStation website.</p>
<h2>Why the country cannot be changed</h2>
<p>Sony says it plainly: an account's country or region cannot be changed after the account is created. The same goes for the wallet: funds stay in the account's currency, and another region's funds cannot be used.</p>
<p>The practical conclusion is simple. Picked the wrong country — you will need a new account. Games and subscriptions bought on the old account stay there.</p>
<h2>A second account and switching users</h2>
<p>Many players keep two accounts: a main one and, say, a Turkish one for local prices. A new account needs its own e-mail address.</p>
<p>Switching between them on the PS5 is easy:</p>
<ol>
<li>Press the PS button on the controller.</li>
<li>Open the Control Center.</li>
<li>Choose switch user and sign in to the second account.</li>
</ol>
<p>Redeem a card on the account whose country matches it. Each account has its own wallet.</p>
<h2>How to redeem a PSN card on PS5</h2>
<ol>
<li>Sign in to the account of the right country.</li>
<li>Open PlayStation Store.</li>
<li>Select «…» at the top of the store and choose Redeem Code.</li>
<li>Enter the code from the card and confirm.</li>
</ol>
<p>The amount appears in the account wallet. Then pay for the game or PS Plus as usual.</p>
<p>Code not accepted? First check which account you are signed in to and whether its country matches the card's. Then check the code itself: an extra space or a mixed-up letter gives the same error.</p>
<h2>How to redeem a card on the web</h2>
<ol>
<li>Open store.playstation.com and sign in to the same account.</li>
<li>Click your avatar and choose Redeem Codes.</li>
<li>Enter the code and confirm.</li>
</ol>
<p>This is handy for topping up the wallet in advance without turning on the console.</p>
<h2>What to check before you buy</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Account country.</strong> Look it up in the settings before buying a card, not from memory.</li>
<li><strong>Card country.</strong> It must match the account country.</li>
<li><strong>Face value.</strong> Will it cover the game at its local price? If not, take two cards or a bigger one.</li>
<li><strong>PS Plus.</strong> The subscription is paid from the wallet of the account it will be on. So the card must be of that account's country too.</li>
<li><strong>Game region.</strong> Some games are region-locked. For example, <a href="/en/blog/how-to-buy-gta-6-in-uzbekistan">GTA 6 codes for PS5</a> work only on an account of the matching region. The safe path is to buy the game in your own account's store.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Common mistakes</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>A card from the wrong country.</strong> The most common one. A Turkish account will not accept a US card, and the other way round. The code is not ruined, but it cannot be credited to that account.</li>
<li><strong>Trying to change the account country.</strong> It is not possible. The only way out is a second account.</li>
<li><strong>Redeeming on the wrong user.</strong> On a console with two accounts, check who is signed in.</li>
<li><strong>Expecting the money to &quot;move&quot;.</strong> One region's funds do not work in another.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How to buy a PSN card on YuPay</h2>
<ol>
<li>Open <a href="/en/store/playstation">PlayStation Store on YuPay</a>.</li>
<li>Choose your account's country, for example <a href="/en/store/playstation?region=tr">Turkey</a> or the <a href="/en/store/playstation?region=us">USA</a>.</li>
<li>Choose a face value.</li>
<li>Pay in soʻm with Click, Payme or Uzum.</li>
<li>The code arrives on the order page and by e-mail.</li>
</ol>
<p>Play on Xbox too? The rules there are different: a Microsoft account country can be changed, with limits. Details in our guide on <a href="/en/blog/how-to-top-up-xbox-from-uzbekistan">how to top up Xbox from Uzbekistan</a>.</p>
<p>Know your account's country? Open <a href="/en/store/playstation">PlayStation Store cards</a>, pick that country and a face value for the game you want.</p>$x$,
  $x$How to buy PS Store games in Uzbekistan — PSN gift cards$x$,
  $x$Buying games and PS Plus in PS Store from Uzbekistan: account country, a PSN card of the right country (Turkey, USA, UAE), redeeming on PS5, common mistakes.$x$
);

